            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all four changed paths in full. The new checkExemptionEvidence in engine/review/app/evidence.go follows the same flow as the existing review-report check: it validates the shape of the record and the ref before locating the repository, reads only the stored file the ref names, and verifies the digest, so a ref that tries to leave the results directory is refused by shape before any read.",
              "The stored exemption is decoded and re-checked against its rules (review.DecodeExemption, review.CheckExemption), so a file edited after the record was made is refused even when the record's digest is changed to match. The range is then checked against the stored binding.",
              "The tests in engine/review/app/exempt_evidence_test.go cover traversal and absolute-path refs, a binding whose base is an option string, tampered digests, and a missing or unreadable store. They show these cases are refused with no git or store call where the shape check applies.",
              "NeedsEvidence in engine/review/evidence.go now also covers completed review-exemption records, and interrupted ones remain exempt, with a test confirming that. This is the requested behavior, and I found no authorization bypass, data exposure, unsafe input handling, secret or dependency risk reachable from this change."
            ]
          }
        }
