            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all four changed paths in full from the patch sections.",
              "NeedsEvidence in engine/review/evidence.go now includes completed review-exemption records; CheckEvidence dispatches to checkExemptionEvidence before the report path, so exemption records are not run through the result/verdict checks.",
              "checkExemptionEvidence in engine/review/app/evidence.go mirrors the report path order: shape checks (RequiredEvidence, ExemptionRef) occur before git.Locate and the store read, then digest check, then decode and rule check wrapped as EvidenceError, then range check against the stored binding. Failure paths are wrapped with kind and ref.",
              "engine/review/app/exempt_evidence_test.go proves: acceptance of the Exempt-printed record with exact git and store calls and no writes, missing/repeated pieces refused before any call, digest and range mismatches, unreadable or missing files, ref-shape refusals with no calls, non-exemption bytes, post-edit rule violations (high risk, invalid risk, not-clear report, bad binding), and interrupted records left alone.",
              "engine/review/exempt_evidence_test.go covers NeedsEvidence for completed, interrupted, case-variant and suffixed kinds.",
              "No reliability regression or unproved behavior found."
            ]
